{"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "Please execute the hyperimmunization, serum testing, and SRID assay validation for our recombinant superoxide dismutase (SOD) project following the steps below:\n\n1. Immunize healthy, brucellosis-seronegative sheep (6\u201312 months old, \u226520 kg) using a prime-boost regimen with 100 \u00b5g of recombinant SOD protein per immunization. Formulate the antigen with either aluminum hydroxide (final concentration 0.2%) or AddaS03 (1:1 v/v ratio). Collect blood samples on days 21, 28, 35, and 42 post-initial immunization to harvest hyperimmune sera.\n\n2. Screen hyperimmune sera via Agar Gel Immunodiffusion (AGID) at 24 \u00b0C using 1% agarose in physiological saline with rivanol against reference Brucella antigen (1:8 titer), using 2-fold serum serial dilutions (1:2 to 1:32) incubated for 24\u201336 hours. Quantify Brucella-specific IgG levels using the MyBioSource Brucella IgG ELISA Kit per manufacturer instructions, measuring OD at 450 nm.\n\n3. Cast 1.5% agarose gels in 0.01 M PBS (pH 7.2\u20137.4) containing monospecific antiserum at 15 \u00b5L/mL, targeting a uniform gel thickness of 2.5\u20133.0 mm.\n\n4. Pre-treat all test samples and standard controls (recombinant human SOD1, Novus Cat. No. NBP2-34940) by mixing with a 10% Zwittergent 3-14 solution at a 1:10 ratio, incubating at room temperature for 30 minutes, then serially diluting in PBS. Load 25 \u00b5L of prepared standard or sample per well.\n\n5. Incubate plates in a humid chamber at room temperature for 24 hours. Wash gels 5 times with PBS (30\u201340 min per wash on an orbital shaker at 40\u201350 rpm), followed by 2 washes in distilled water (15 min each under same shaking conditions). Stain gels with 0.3% Coomassie Brilliant Blue G-250 and destain with acetic acid/ethanol until distinct precipitation rings are clear.\n\n6. Measure precipitation ring diameters (D) to 0.1 mm precision, calculate the square of the diameter (D\u00b2), and perform assay validation according to the following parameters:\n   - Specificity: Test target SOD1 at 20, 10, and 5 \u00b5g/mL alongside negative/heterologous controls (OMP16, OMP19, L7/L12, IalB, BSA, and PBS) in triplicate (n=3). Confirm ring formation occurs exclusively with target SOD1.\n   - Sensitivity: Test 2-fold serial dilutions of SOD1 from 10 to 0.078 \u00b5g/mL in triplicate (n=3). Determine the Limit of Detection (LOD) as the lowest concentration yielding symmetrical, reproducible rings with CV \u2264 10%.\n   - Linearity: Analyze concentrations from 10 to 0.625 \u00b5g/mL in triplicate (n=3). Perform linear regression of D\u00b2 versus concentration and report R\u00b2 (acceptability criterion: R\u00b2 \u2265 0.95).\n   - Precision: Run 3 independent assay series with 3 replicates each (n=9 total per level) at 20 \u00b5g/mL and 5 \u00b5g/mL SOD1. Confirm CV \u2264 10%.\n   - Robustness: Test SOD1 at 20 and 5 \u00b5g/mL in triplicate under deliberate parameter variations: temperature (25 \u00b1 3 \u00b0C), gel thickness (2.5\u20133.0 mm), and incubation time (20\u201324 h). Confirm CV remains \u2264 10%.\n\n7. Provide a final data summary reporting D_mean, D\u00b2_mean, SD, CV (%), linear regression curves with R\u00b2 values, and calculated sample concentrations based on standard calibration curves.", "thoughtSignature": ""}], "role": "model"}, "finishReason": "STOP", "index": 0}], "usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 2535, "candidatesTokenCount": 886, "totalTokenCount": 5415, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 2535}], "thoughtsTokenCount": 1994, "serviceTier": "standard"}, "modelVersion": "gemini-3.6-flash", "responseId": "-Kz2aq2PLrqj1MkPtPPWuQM"}